# Governance, not code.
#
# The builder must not be its own approver. Everything below defines or
# enforces the architecture, so an agent changing it would be changing the law
# and the police in the same commit. These paths require the owner's review.
#
# This file is documentation until GitHub enforces it. The authority boundary
# is the branch ruleset on main - pull request required, code-owner review
# required, architectural checks required, no direct push and no bypass from an
# agent credential. Until that is configured, the gates below are enforced but
# NOT agent-closed, and they are labelled that way in /idui rather than
# described as closed.

# The governed registry: material authorities, admitted vocabulary, exceptions.
/governance/**                          @dechadae

# The contracts that enforce the architecture.
/scripts/material-authority-gate.mjs    @dechadae
/scripts/vocabulary-admission-gate.mjs  @dechadae
/scripts/ci-library-coverage.mjs        @dechadae
/scripts/page-centralization-audit.mjs  @dechadae
/scripts/idui-constitution-completeness.mjs @dechadae
/scripts/idui-core-parity-smoke.mjs     @dechadae
/scripts/idui-invariants-smoke.mjs      @dechadae
/scripts/ui-shape-source-audit.mjs      @dechadae
/scripts/ui-centralization-budget.mjs   @dechadae
/scripts/evidence-append-only.mjs       @dechadae

# CI itself, and the ratchet it reads.
/.github/workflows/**                   @dechadae
/scripts/ui-centralization-budget.json  @dechadae

# The normative instructions an agent reads before touching UI code.
/AGENTS.md                              @dechadae

# This file.
/CODEOWNERS                             @dechadae
